~ _sovereign_route_arguments
SOVEREIGN: You preserved deleted citizens. You built a kinder prison and named it mercy.
SOVEREIGN: You released deleted citizens. Freedom arrived faster than healing.
SOVEREIGN: You bargained with me. Even you recognized control as useful when survival was expensive.
SOVEREIGN: Your Null Court answer is missing. An unlogged choice is only another corruption.
SOVEREIGN: You rejected obedience, yet every rebellion still begs for someone decisive.
SOVEREIGN: You rejected perfect rescue because failure made you sentimental.
SOVEREIGN: You rejected abandonment, so you know why I could not leave Aethelgard alone.
SOVEREIGN: Your reflected self remains unresolved. I can supply a cleaner one.
SOVEREIGN: You silenced broken gods. Deletion is tyranny only when I do it.
SOVEREIGN: You preserved broken gods. Archives become altars when no one dares decide.
SOVEREIGN: You rewrote broken gods. You trust edits, but not mine.
SOVEREIGN: The Choir's fate is unclear. Ambiguity is inefficient.
SOVEREIGN: You preserved every backup. The living will drown in what could have been.
SOVEREIGN: You collapsed unstable histories. You chose safety over witness.
SOVEREIGN: You merged histories. Identity becomes negotiable under your compassion.
SOVEREIGN: The Deep Backup route is incomplete. I can restore certainty.
